{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ישגו", :translit "yishgu", :gloss "they err"} {:he "ואם כל עדת ישראל ישגו", :translit "ve'im kol adat yisra'el yishgu", :gloss "and if the whole congregation of Israel errs"} {:he "ישגו צאני", :translit "yishgu tsonai", :gloss "they err, my flock"} {:he "המתעים את הצאן", :translit "hamati'im et ha-tson", :gloss "who mislead the flock"} {:he "שטעו בהוראה", :translit "she-ta'u be-hora'ah", :gloss "who erred in a ruling"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואם כל עדת ישראל ישגו" "ישגו צאני"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase ישגו צאני appears in Ezekiel 34:6–8, where the prophet rebukes the shepherds of Israel for misleading the flock. The parallel usage of 'erring' establishes that Leviticus 4:13, which addresses the whole congregation of Israel erring, refers specifically to an erroneous ruling issued by the Sanhedrin, as defined in Horayot 2a–3a.", :sources ["Ezekiel 34:6" "Ezekiel 34:8" "Horayot 2a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מעיני", :translit "me'einei", :gloss "from the eyes of"} {:he "ונעלם דבר מעיני הקהל", :translit "vene'lam davar me'einei ha-qahal", :gloss "and the matter was hidden from the eyes of the congregation"} {:he "אם מעיני העדה", :translit "im me'einei ha-edah", :gloss "if from the eyes of the congregation"} {:he "ונעלם מעיני אישה", :translit "vene'lam me'einei ishah", :gloss "and it was hidden from the eyes of her husband"} {:he "ונעלמ' מעיני כל חי", :translit "une'lamah me'einei kol chai", :gloss "and it was hidden from the eyes of all living"} {:he "והחכמה מאין תמצא", :translit "ve-hachmah me'ayin timatze", :gloss "and wisdom, from where is it found"} {:he "שנטמאה שוב אין המים בודקין אותה", :translit "she-nitme'ah shuv ein ha-mayim bodqin otah", :gloss "that she was defiled, again the waters do not test her"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ונעלם דבר מעיני הקהל" "מעיני העדה" "מעיני אישה" "מעיני כל חי"]}], :frame {:text "The verse preceding Job 28:12 (והחכמה מאין תמצא) is Job 28:20–21, which states that wisdom is hidden from the eyes of all living (ונעלמה מעיני כל חי) and from the birds of the sky (ומעוף השמים). Ba'al HaTurim reads this as a veiled allusion to the court's failed legal wisdom. The sotah law appears in Sotah 28b and Mishnah Sotah 3:4: if the woman was definitively warned, even second-hand (compared to hearing from a flying bird), the waters no longer test her. The phrase מעיני אישה is drawn from Numbers 5:13 in the sotah passage.", :sources ["Job 28:12" "Job 28:20" "Job 28:21" "Numbers 5:13" "Sotah 28b" "Mishnah Sotah 3:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואם כל עדת ישראל ישגו" "ישגו צאני"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואם כל עדת ישראל ישגו", :refs ["Leviticus 4:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ישגו צאני", :refs ["Ezekiel 34:6"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ונעלם דבר מעיני הקהל" "מעיני העדה" "מעיני אישה" "מעיני כל חי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ונעלם דבר מעיני הקהל", :refs ["Leviticus 4:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מעיני העדה", :refs ["Numbers 15:24"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מעיני אישה", :refs ["Numbers 5:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מעיני כל חי", :refs ["Job 28:21"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:07.325959109Z", :model "glm-5.2"}